From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:43:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: give an unbound shader image its own empty image unit

A shader image that carries no bound resource has to read as zero, and
OpenGL reaches that state routinely: binding a texture level that does not
exist leaves the image unit invalid, and the guest then hands us a null
resource for that slot.

vrend_draw_bind_images_shader() skipped such a slot entirely.  On desktop GL
the image is declared as layout(location=N) uniform imageT, so the shader
reads the image unit named by that uniform, and an image uniform that is
never written keeps its default value of zero.  The shader therefore
addressed image unit 0 and read whichever resource was bound there -- the
first image of the same draw, in the usual case.

Walk the images the linked program declares instead of only the ones with a
resource, and point every unbound image at its own image unit with nothing
bound to it.  KHR-GL46.shader_image_load_store.incomplete_textures covers
this: it binds a complete image to unit 0 and a level that does not exist to
units 2 and 3, then requires imageLoad from the latter to return zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 8b75c9d0e4816f2093d2d49e8566495b112185df..1885376799e6cccd4402b61607ffcfeec06d1c1d 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -5556,8 +5556,7 @@ static void vrend_draw_bind_images_shader(struct vrend_sub_context *sub_ctx, int
    struct vrend_image_view *iview;
    uint32_t mask, tex_id, level, first_layer;
 
-
-   if (!sub_ctx->images_used_mask[shader_type])
+   if (!sub_ctx->prog->images_used_mask[shader_type])
       return;
 
    if (!sub_ctx->prog->img_locs[shader_type])
@@ -5566,6 +5565,28 @@ static void vrend_draw_bind_images_shader(struct vrend_sub_context *sub_ctx, int
    if (!has_feature(feat_images))
       return;
 
+   /* An image the shader declares but that has no resource bound has to read
+    * as zero.  Its uniform is never written below, and an image uniform starts
+    * out as 0, so leaving it alone makes the shader address image unit 0 and
+    * read whatever that unit holds.  Point every such image at its own unit and
+    * leave the unit empty instead. */
+   uint32_t unbound = sub_ctx->prog->images_used_mask[shader_type] &
+                      ~sub_ctx->images_used_mask[shader_type];
+   while (unbound) {
+      unsigned i = u_bit_scan(&unbound);
+      int image_unit = i + sub_ctx->prog->ss[shader_type]->sel->sinfo.image_binding_offset;
+      int binding = sub_ctx->prog->img_locs[shader_type][i];
+
+      if (binding == -1)
+         continue;
+
+      if (!vrend_state.use_gles)
+         glUniform1i(image_unit, binding);
+
+      glBindImageTexture(vrend_state.use_gles ? image_unit : binding, 0, 0,
+                         GL_FALSE, 0, GL_READ_ONLY, GL_R32UI);
+   }
+
    mask = sub_ctx->images_used_mask[shader_type] & sub_ctx->prog->images_used_mask[shader_type];
 
    while (mask) {
